  "overview": "I use computational and quantitative methods to investigate disease initiation, progression, and therapeutic resistance as a biologist. I have previously worked as a computational research scientist at St. Jude and conducted postdoctoral research in population and quantitative genetics at the University of Texas, Austin. I have focused on bioinformatics and genomics at Notre Dame, particularly infectious diseases. I also have an ecology and evolutionary biology research background at UCLA and completed my undergraduate studies in cell biology and genetics at Peking University (Beijing University).",
